properties.description:
This check runs crates/reflow2-mcp/tests/every_skill_is_found_by_a_query_in_the_users_words.rs, whose corpus now holds a query for hub in a person's words ("someone dropped an idea into the space we share for all our projects, decide which one it belongs in and put it there"). It asserts four things:
- hub is served;
- hub has a corpus query;
- hub is in find_skills' top five for that query;
- hub is ranked FIRST, not in the not_first baseline.
tools/skill_lint.py and tools/check_command_surface.py check the rest of its contract: frontmatter, the standing rule, every backticked term served or allowlisted, the WRITES and MINTS obligations, byte-identical mirrors, and a /hub command naming it. It does not check whether an agent following the skill files facts in the right design; only a real hub session can show that.
